<p> Full listing of the content of the galaxy sizes table and description of
the columns. These properties are contained in tables denoted
[modelname]_Sizes. This table contains half-mass sizes of the stellar component
of galaxies using spherical apertures. The GalaxyID column can be used to join
this table to the corresponding [modelname]_SubHalo table. Only galaxies with
total stellar mass M<sub>*</sub> > 10<sup>8</sup> Msol have entries in this
table. </p>

<table>
<tr><th align='left'>Field</th><th align='left'>Units</th><th align='left'>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><p>GalaxyID</p></td><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Unique ID of this galaxy, corresponding to the GalaxyID in the SubHalo table.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td><p>R_halfmass30</p></td><td><p>pkpc</p></td><td><p>Half mass radius computed for mass within a spherical 30 pkpc aperture.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td><p>R_halfmass100</p></td><td><p>pkpc</p></td><td><p>Half mass radius computed for mass within a spherical 100 pkpc aperture.</p></td></tr>
<tr><td><p>R_halfmass30_projected</p></td><td><p>pkpc</p></td><td><p>Projected half mass radius computed for mass within a 30 pkpc aperture (averaged over three orthogonal projections).</p></td></tr>
<tr><td><p>R_halfmass100_projected</p></td><td><p>pkpc</p></td><td><p>Projected half mass radius computed for mass within a 100 pkpc aperture (averaged over three orthogonal projections).</p></td></tr>
</table>

